Print one entity's full field schema: types, operators, required, relations.

Every field entry carries the same 26 keys, using null or the sentinels "n/a" /
"unknown" where a fact could not be learned, so `jq '.data.fields[] |
select(.required)'` is total and never needs a presence check.

SYNOPSIS
  pay describe <collection|global> [--field PATH] [--required-only] [--queryable] [--examples] [--sample]

DISCOVERED IN THIS PROJECT
  profile=default base_url=- discovery_revision=-
  cache is cold — run 'pay discover' to populate

FLAGS
    --examples                   add generated, copy-pasteable commands for this entity
    --field FIELD                describe one field path in full (dotted, e.g. hero.links.link.url)
    -h, --help                   help for describe
    --queryable                  only fields usable in --where
    --required-only              only fields whose required is known true
    --sample                     also fetch one real document (one extra request)

  Root flags (every command): run 'pay --help' for the full list.
    --profile --base-url --output --path --quiet --verbose --timeout --deadline
    --no-cache --refresh --yes --dry-run --no-audit --no-redact --errors-to

OUTPUT
  data_kind: schema
  .data = {"kind":"collection","entity":{…},"fields":[{"path":"title","payload_type":"text","required":true,"queryable":true,"operators":["equals","contains",…]}],"required_paths":["title"]}
  Envelope: {"ok":true,"v":1,"command":"…","data_kind":"…","data":…,"meta":{…},"warnings":[]}

EXIT CODES
    0   success
    2   auth — missing, invalid, locked or unverifiable credential
    6   network — DNS, TLS, timeout or a 5xx from the server
    9   configuration — no base_url, unknown profile, secret in plaintext
    10  capability — this project does not support the operation
  
  Full table: pay explain --section exit_codes

EXAMPLES
  # everything about a collection
  pay describe pages

  # what must I supply to create one?
  pay describe pages --required-only --path .fields[].path

  # what can I filter on?
  pay describe pages --queryable --path .queryable_paths[]

  # one field in full, including its operators
  pay describe pages --field title

  # the blockTypes a blocks field accepts
  pay describe pages --field layout

  # schema plus a real document
  pay describe pages --sample

  # generated commands for this collection
  pay describe pages --examples --path .examples[]


COMMON MISTAKES
  1. Reading `required: null` as "not required".
     Instead: null means PayCLI never learned it. Attempt the write; a 400 names the missing fields precisely.
  2. Using a join field in --select.
     Instead: Join fields are read-only and are requested with --joins 'field:limit=5,sort=-createdAt'; .join_fields lists them.
  3. Assuming `sortable: true` was measured.
     Instead: Sortability is heuristic unless sortable_confidence says otherwise; Payload silently ignores an unsortable field.
  4. Expecting `blocks` to be filled on every project.
     Instead: Block slugs are not in the API; a null means no source resolved them. .blocks_source says which source did.

SEE ALSO
  pay collections
  pay explain --collection <slug>
  pay find <collection> --select …

